Deliberation history: Round 0 had colleagues split mainly between D and E/K. In round 1, all colleagues moved to favor D, citing D’s full 20-nt length and favorable CGG PAM versus the 19-nt E/K as written. No substantive dissent remains. Unresolved caveat: if E/K are typographical truncations rather than intended 19-nt spacers, E corrected could be a viable exon-2 guide, but D still remains the best literal answer and best off-target guess.}

